.TH EXTRACT 1 "August 2026" "pack-extract 1.5.4" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
extract \- automatically extract compressed archives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B extract
.RB [ \-v | \-\-version ]
.br
.B extract
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.br
.B extract
.I archive
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B extract
opens
.I archive
with
.BR libarchive (3)
(all supported formats and filters) and writes members into the current
directory. After a successful extraction it prints a sorted list of
extracted paths.
.PP
Absolute member paths and path components equal to
.B ..
are rejected to mitigate zip-slip style traversal.
.PP
If a member path already exists in the current directory,
.B extract
asks whether to overwrite or replace it
.RB ( y / N ).
Answer
.B n
(or Enter) to skip that member.
.B Ctrl+C
cancels the whole extraction.
Existing directories that match a directory member are merged without prompting.
In non-interactive mode (stdin/stdout not a tty), a conflict aborts with an error.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Display help message and exit.
.SH SUPPORTED FORMATS
Anything
.B libarchive
can read with
.B archive_read_support_format_all
and
.B archive_read_support_filter_all
on the build host, typically including tar (with gzip, xz, bzip2, zstd,
lz4, lzip, lzop, brotli when available), zip, 7z, cpio, and common
single-file compression streams.
.PP
Exact coverage depends on how
.B libarchive
was built (optional codecs).
.SH EXAMPLES
Extract a gzip-compressed tarball:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ extract backup.tar.gz
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract a zip file:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ extract project.zip
.fi
.RE
.PP
Extract a 7z archive:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ extract data.7z
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful extraction.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred (file not found, unsafe path, unsupported or corrupt
archive, I/O failure).
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B extract
links against
.BR libarchive (3).
Build requires the libarchive development package and
.BR pkg-config (1).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pack (1),
.BR libarchive (3)
